; LANPARTY: the script the Amiga runs when it boots. AROS's built-in shell reads it.
; Only the shell's own commands exist here (Echo, Alias, Prompt, Ask, If...). *E is an escape, *N a new line.
; Build the disk with: python3 tools/make-amiga-disk.py
Prompt "A500> "
Echo "*E[7m LAN PARTY '98 *E[0m  the Amiga corner"
Echo ""
Echo "Amiga 500, one floppy drive, a mouse, a joystick port with nothing in it."
Echo "Kickstart is AROS, which is open source. The emulator is PUAE."
Echo "This disk holds a Startup-Sequence and nothing else."
Echo "Workbench is on the other disk. Dazza has it. Dazza is not here."
Echo ""
Echo "Type *E[7mHELP*E[0m."
Echo ""
Alias help Echo "HELP  DAZZA  VOLT  GURU  BOING  ENDCLI*NThat is everything this disk knows."
Alias dazza Echo "Dazza says Workbench is at his place. He will bring it round after the footy."
Alias volt Echo "No Volt Cola in the disk drive. Cans do not fit. Mum asked."
Alias guru Echo "Software Failure.   Press left mouse button to continue.*NGuru Meditation #00000004.0000AAC0"
Alias boing Echo "Boing."
